{
  $schema: "https://docs.renovatebot.com/renovate-schema.json",
  extends: [
    ":timezone(Europe/Warsaw)",

    "local>deedee/mark13//.renovate/homeOpsBase.json5",
    "local>deedee/mark13//.renovate/homeOpsApps.json5",

    "local>deedee/mark13//.renovate/autoMerge.json5",
    "local>deedee/mark13//.renovate/customManagers.json5",
    "local>deedee/mark13//.renovate/exclusions.json5",
    "local>deedee/mark13//.renovate/groups.json5",
    "local>deedee/mark13//.renovate/labels.json5",
    "local>deedee/mark13//.renovate/talosFactory.json5",
  ],
  packageRules: [
    {
      description: "Map terraform registry to opentofu",
      matchDatasources: ["terraform-provider", "terraform-module"],
      registryUrls: ["https://registry.opentofu.org"],
    },
    {
      description: "ncps changes its migration mechanism across minors -- never merge unreviewed",
      matchDatasources: ["docker"],
      matchPackageNames: ["/kalbasit\\/ncps/"],
      matchUpdateTypes: ["major", "minor"],
      automerge: false,
      prBodyNotes: [
        "⚠️ **`docker/ncps/compose.yaml` must be updated in this PR.**",
        "**1. Migrations (blocking).** The `ncps-init` service applies migrations with `/bin/dbmate`, which v0.10 removes from the image entirely (binary, wrapper package and the `NCPS_DB_*` env), replacing it with a built-in goose migrator that adopts the dbmate-shaped `schema_migrations` table on first run. Merging without swapping the command for `/bin/ncps migrate up --cache-database-url=sqlite:/var/lib/ncps/db.sqlite` leaves `ncps-init` failing with `exec: \"/bin/dbmate\": no such file or directory`, and `ncps` will not start.",
        "**2. Eviction (deferred until now on purpose).** The cache currently grows without bound: `--cache-max-size` and `--cache-lru-schedule` are deliberately unset, because 0.9.x LRU sorts purely on `last_accessed_at` with no exemptions. ncps only bumps that timestamp when it *serves* a path, and flake inputs are read from each machine's local nix store during evaluation -- so they are served ~never, sit at the bottom of the LRU ordering, and would be evicted first, silently destroying the ability to evaluate the flake offline.",
        "v0.10 adds the pin API, which is the fix: `POST /pin/{hash}.narinfo` exempts a closure *and everything it depends on* from eviction. Pin each host's `system.build.toplevel` plus the flake archive root, verify via `GET /pins`, and only then set `--cache-max-size` and a weekly `--cache-lru-schedule` (the LRU cron job is only registered when a schedule is given, and setting one requires a max size).",
        "Nothing about eviction is urgent -- if storage is still comfortable, it is fine to take the migration fix in this PR and leave the cache unbounded. Just do not enable a size cap without pinning first.",
      ],
    },
  ],
}
